106
00:11:42,770 --> 00:11:49,650
At that time, I didn’t learn much Korean.

107
00:11:49,650 --> 00:11:56,650
But I really like Korean culture.

108
00:11:56,650 --> 00:12:07,070
I also like cooking Korean food like kimchi stew or jajangmyeon.

109
00:12:07,070 --> 00:12:27,830
Recently, I met a Korean person, and thanks to that person, I want to study Korean harder.

110
00:12:27,830 --> 00:12:34,040
That person is a skilled musician.

111
00:12:34,040 --> 00:12:36,930
A person who does music.

112
00:12:36,930 --> 00:12:43,850
Can I call that person “musician-nim”?

113
00:12:43,850 --> 00:12:47,700
Korean legal drama.

114
00:12:47,700 --> 00:13:00,580
In Korean legal dramas, prosecutors or lawyers are called “lawyer-nim”...

115
00:13:00,580 --> 00:13:06,340
So I thought it might be okay to call like that.

116
00:13:06,340 --> 00:13:11,740
Keep up the good work on your YouTube channel!

117
00:13:11,740 --> 00:13:15,070
Thank you, Justin!

118
00:13:15,070 --> 00:13:21,650
It’s amazing that you lived in Pohang.

119
00:13:21,650 --> 00:13:28,500
Pohang is a city close to Busan.

120
00:13:28,500 --> 00:13:31,670
You all know Busan, right?

121
00:13:31,670 --> 00:13:38,300
Recently, traveling to Busan in Korea has become very popular.

122
00:13:38,300 --> 00:13:46,160
I’m Korean too, but I haven’t been to Pohang yet.

123
00:13:46,160 --> 00:13:53,280
I’ve been to Busan but not Pohang yet.

124
00:13:53,280 --> 00:14:04,060
Pohang is a city famous for its beautiful sea and seafood.

125
00:14:04,060 --> 00:14:06,180
Seafood.

126
00:14:06,180 --> 00:14:16,570
