158
00:18:14,430 --> 00:18:20,330
In Korean, this is called “dongmyeongiin.”

159
00:18:20,330 --> 00:18:25,660
Dongmyeongiin.

160
00:18:25,660 --> 00:18:30,370
Same name but different person.

161
00:18:30,370 --> 00:18:32,860
Dongmyeongiin.

162
00:18:32,860 --> 00:18:37,920
Anyway, nice to meet you, Anya.

163
00:18:37,920 --> 00:18:44,330
This person wrote an email in Korean.

164
00:18:44,330 --> 00:18:55,200
From now on, I will make slight corrections to emails written in Korean.

165
00:18:55,200 --> 00:19:16,370
It’s very well written and perfect, but since this is a slow podcast, I will make it a bit more casual, easier, and comfortable Korean.

166
00:19:16,370 --> 00:19:19,000
Hello, Ria.

167
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:23,140
This is Anya living in Russia.

168
00:19:23,140 --> 00:19:35,100
I was hesitating whether to write a story after seeing your YouTube post, but I gathered courage and sent it.

169
00:19:35,100 --> 00:19:40,860
I’m a bit shy, but I think it’s a good challenge.

170
00:19:40,860 --> 00:19:51,460
Actually, studying Korean was not just a hobby for me.

171
00:19:51,460 --> 00:19:53,680
It was therapy.

172
00:19:53,680 --> 00:19:55,260
Therapy.

173
00:19:55,260 --> 00:20:08,370
I can’t say in detail, but I was mentally very troubled and lonely in the past.

174
00:20:08,370 --> 00:20:12,930
I didn’t have peace of mind.

175
00:20:12,930 --> 00:20:20,090
So I wanted to change my life.

176
00:20:20,090 --> 00:20:34,230
At that time, I was deeply into K-pop, and suddenly I thought, “How about studying Korean?”

177
00:20:34,230 --> 00:20:40,480
That’s how I started studying Korean.

178
00:20:40,480 --> 00:20:55,450
As time passed, my heart gradually healed, and I developed affection for Korean.

179
00:20:55,450 --> 00:21:03,390
I’m really glad I studied Korean then.

180
00:21:03,390 --> 00:21:11,750
If I hadn’t, I wouldn’t have gotten better this quickly.

181
00:21:11,750 --> 00:21:20,680
That choice completely changed my life.

182
00:21:20,680 --> 00:21:33,570
Even if I go back to the past, I would definitely study Korean again.

183
00:21:33,570 --> 00:21:38,590
Thank you, Anya, for your courage.

184
00:21:38,590 --> 00:21:43,950
You’ve been through a lot.

185
00:21:43,950 --> 00:21:49,730
I’m glad you’re much better now.

186
00:21:49,730 --> 00:21:59,650
And I’m so happy that Korean has helped you a lot!

187
00:21:59,650 --> 00:22:10,260
For you, studying Korean was not just a hobby but therapy.

188
00:22:10,260 --> 00:22:12,070
Therapy.

189
00:22:12,070 --> 00:22:21,270
Starting to study Korean then was really the best choice.

190
00:22:21,270 --> 00:22:24,080
The best choice, right?

191
00:22:24,080 --> 00:22:38,350
And now, I’m even happier that we can study and communicate together on my channel.

192
00:22:38,350 --> 00:22:43,660
I’m really so happy! Thank you.

193
00:22:43,660 --> 00:22:54,520
When I’m struggling and don’t have peace of mind, I try to do something new.

194
00:22:54,520 --> 00:23:10,110
I start a new hobby, study a language, play chess, or try to think about something else.

195
00:23:10,110 --> 00:23:15,420
For me, that study was English.

196
00:23:15,420 --> 00:23:18,110
That language was English.

197
00:23:18,110 --> 00:23:25,020
English changed my life a lot.

198
00:23:25,020 --> 00:23:34,240
Like Anya, if I go back to the past, I would study English again.

199
00:23:34,240 --> 00:23:46,070
Actually, I’m still studying now, but if I go back, I think I would study more and harder.

200
00:23:46,070 --> 00:23:51,880
Anyway, I really relate to this.

201
00:23:51,880 --> 00:23:53,760
I can relate.

202
00:23:53,760 --> 00:24:03,310
I will continue to support Anya's Korean studies that changed her life.

203
00:24:03,310 --> 00:24:16,590
I hope K-pop and my videos become good energy for you in both hard times and happy times.

204
00:24:16,590 --> 00:24:22,880
I hope it becomes good energy for all of you.

205
00:24:22,880 --> 00:24:34,440
Anya, take care of your health and let's continue to enjoy studying together. Fighting!

206
