279
00:33:20,200 --> 00:33:21,730
You are really good!

280
00:33:21,730 --> 00:33:27,850
Anyway, I will continue to support you. Fighting!

281
00:33:27,850 --> 00:33:36,120
Next story is from Jan Justin.

282
00:33:36,120 --> 00:33:41,410
It doesn't say which country he is from.

283
00:33:41,410 --> 00:33:47,780
Hello, Teacher Lia! This is Jan Justin.

284
00:33:47,780 --> 00:33:56,950
Your channel already has over 50,000 subscribers.

285
00:33:56,950 --> 00:34:01,020
Congratulations sincerely.

286
00:34:01,020 --> 00:34:19,520
Actually, from elementary school to middle school, I knew nothing about Korean language or culture and had no interest.

287
00:34:19,520 --> 00:34:42,520
I was just a student who studied hard, but later I had many worries because I had no dream about what kind of person I wanted to become.

288
00:34:42,520 --> 00:34:54,080
Then, in high school, during a Boy Scout camping trip, I went to a tree planting event.

289
00:34:54,080 --> 00:35:03,550
There, I met a pretty Korean woman and a handsome man.

290
00:35:03,550 --> 00:35:16,180
Those two people helped me a lot when I was having a hard time during camping.

291
00:35:16,180 --> 00:35:27,160
I wanted to say thank you, but I couldn't because I didn't know Korean.

292
00:35:27,160 --> 00:35:34,530
From then on, I started studying Korean.

293
00:35:34,530 --> 00:35:45,140
As I studied, I found it more interesting than I thought and became more interested.

294
00:35:45,140 --> 00:35:59,290
I gradually got into K-pop, Korean songs, dramas, and also started to like Korean food.

295
00:35:59,290 --> 00:36:10,620
I got addicted to studying Korean and worked hard, and now I have come this far.

296
00:36:10,620 --> 00:36:18,590
Especially Admiral Yi Sun-sin from Korean history is also my favorite.

297
00:36:18,590 --> 00:36:25,780
While learning Korean, I found something I want to do.

298
00:36:25,780 --> 00:36:38,940
Someday, I want to study abroad at a Korean university and later become a lawyer in Korea.

299
00:36:38,940 --> 00:37:01,940
Right now, I have enough skills to understand Teacher Lia's podcast, but I want to study harder to speak fluently without any difficulty.

300
00:37:01,940 --> 00:37:08,590
Teacher Lia, once again, congratulations on 50,000 subscribers.

301
00:37:08,590 --> 00:37:19,190
I will always be a subscriber who supports you until the very end.

302
00:37:19,190 --> 00:37:24,510
Thank you so much!

303
00:37:24,510 --> 00:37:35,250
You started studying Korean thanks to the Korean people you met while camping.

304
00:37:35,250 --> 00:37:39,960
That's a really special reason, right?

305
00:37:39,960 --> 00:37:46,960
Justin! I'm really curious about which country you met them in.

306
00:37:46,960 --> 00:37:59,460
And it's so cute that you said Admiral Yi Sun-sin is your favorite in Korean history.

307
00:37:59,460 --> 00:38:08,160
Usually, the term 'favorite' (최애) is used a lot for idol members.

308
00:38:08,160 --> 00:38:21,420
But using the expression 'favorite' for such a very old historical figure is so adorable.

309
00:38:21,420 --> 00:38:32,810
Anyway, I hope you, Jen, will definitely come to Korea someday and make that dream come true.

310
00:38:32,810 --> 00:38:45,350
I will upload more good videos in the future so you can speak Korean fluently.

311
00:38:45,350 --> 00:38:54,460
Let's continue to study together in a fun way, okay? Fighting!

312
00:38:54,460 --> 00:39:00,140
